<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xliff xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:2.0" xmlns:swi18n="https://step-wise.com/ns/i18n" version="2.1" srcLang="en" trgLang="de">
	<file id="catalog">
		<group id="meta">
			<unit id="learningGoals">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">This skill focuses on <pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">adding two numbers</pc>. It builds up to to a combined skill where we both <pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:skill-link" swi18n:slot="children">add and multiply numbers</pc>.</pc></source>
					<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="43492d633ad37b54" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="5a0dc0d9b6e97ecb"><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Diese Kompetenz konzentriert sich auf das <pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">Addieren zweier Zahlen</pc>. Sie baut auf einer kombinierten Kompetenz auf, bei der wir <pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:skill-link" swi18n:slot="children">Zahlen addieren und multiplizieren</pc>.</pc></target>
				</segment>
			</unit>
		</group>
		<group id="theory">
			<unit id="intro">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Yet another basic skill is the skill of adding numbers. This is our last step in preparing for combined skills.</pc></source>
					<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="e58a3bd66ba9be42" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="94141ced550f4025"><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Eine weitere Grundkompetenz ist das Addieren von Zahlen. Dies ist der letzte Schritt in der Vorbereitung auf eine kombinierte Kompetenz.</pc></target>
				</segment>
			</unit>
			<unit id="addNumbers">
				<segment>
					<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:head" swi18n:slot="children">Adding numbers</pc><pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">In this skill you have to <pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">add two numbers</pc>. It's a tutorial - you're allowed to use your calculator - but see if you can do without.</pc><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">When calculating a sum, for instance <ph id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>, you can do the following steps.</pc><pc id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:list" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c7" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">First add the two rightmost numbers. So <ph id="c8" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> becomes <ph id="c9" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>. The latter digit - the <ph id="c10" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> - shows the rightmost digit of our result.</pc><pc id="c11" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Then add the two second numbers. So <ph id="c12" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> becomes <ph id="c13" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>. This is the second digit of our result. Except: if our first digit was <ph id="c14" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> or more (which in our example it was) then we carry over that <ph id="c15" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> and add it here. So we'd get <ph id="c16" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> here.</pc><pc id="c17" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Merge the two results together to get the final result: <ph id="c18" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c19" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Try it out yourself!</pc></source>
					<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="5fd258b30ec2cc0d" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="2a8e0cb924eb4f94"><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:head" swi18n:slot="children">Zahlen addieren</pc><pc id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Bei dieser Kompetenz geht es darum, <pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:term" swi18n:slot="children">zwei Zahlen zu addieren</pc>. Es ist ein Tutorial - du darfst deinen Taschenrechner benutzen - aber schau, ob du es auch ohne schaffst.</pc><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Bei der Berechnung einer Addition, z. B. <ph id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>, führt man die folgenden Schritte aus.</pc><pc id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:list" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c7" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Zuerst addiert man die beiden rechten Zahlen. So wird <ph id="c8" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> zu <ph id="c9" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>. Die letzte Ziffer - die <ph id="c10" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> - ist die rechte Ziffer deines Endergebnisses.</pc><pc id="c11" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Danach addierst du die beiden zweiten Zahlen. So wird <ph id="c12" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> zu <ph id="c13" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>. Das ist die zweite Zahl deines Endergebnisses. Nur: Wenn unsere erste Zahl <ph id="c14" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> oder mehr war (was in unserem Beispiel der Fall war), dann übertragen wir diese <ph id="c15" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> und addieren sie hier. Wir erhalten dann <ph id="c16" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/> hier.</pc><pc id="c17" type="ui" subType="swi18n:item" swi18n:slot="children">Füge die beiden Ergebnisse zusammen, um die endgültige Antwort zu erhalten: <ph id="c18" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc></pc><pc id="c19" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Probier es selbst aus!</pc></target>
				</segment>
			</unit>
		</group>
		<group id="practice">
			<group id="summation1">
				<unit id="problem">
					<segment>
						<source><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Calculate the addition <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc><pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:input-space" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:integer-input"><pc id="x1" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="label">Answer</pc><pc id="x2" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="prelabel"><ph id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/></pc></pc></pc></pc></source>
						<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="6abb0f2f222343ad" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="645be15b53f8f488"><pc id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children">Berechne die Summe <ph id="c2" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</pc><pc id="c3" type="ui" subType="swi18n:input-space" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c4" type="ui" subType="swi18n:par" swi18n:slot="children"><pc id="c5" type="ui" subType="swi18n:integer-input"><pc id="x1" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="label">Antwort</pc><pc id="x2" type="other" subType="swi18n:slot" swi18n:name="prelabel"><ph id="c6" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/></pc></pc></pc></pc></target>
					</segment>
				</unit>
				<unit id="solution">
					<segment>
						<source>The solution is <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</source>
						<target swi18n:sourceContentFingerprint="8cb376d2c35d63de" swi18n:sourceStructureFingerprint="8c52ffd8f6d33b16">Die Lösung ist <ph id="c1" type="ui" subType="swi18n:inline-math"/>.</target>
					</segment>
				</unit>
			</group>
		</group>
